  "body": "Found by #77. The kernel's hop rule between stations a quarter turn apart assumes each hole sits on its station's centre line. An (8,-6)/(-6,8) pair on an r10 bar passes 10.757 mm from the spindle, putting an r2 drill's edge 1.24 mm inside the bar. #77's rapid proof refuses it by name (safe), but the kernel should raise the hop instead.\n\nDone means: the hop height accounts for off-centre holes so such pairs post clear; pinned by that (8,-6)/(-6,8) case.",
